{'symbol': 'DUK', 'date': '2020-02-15 05:30:00', 'title': 'Hydrodec Group Reports FY Revenue $11.6 Million Versus $14.9 Million', 'text': "FY REVENUE 11.6 MILLION USD VERSUS 14.9 MILLION USD YEAR AGO.YEAR-END TRADING UPDATE.FY REVENUES APPROXIMATELY US$11.6 MILLION (2018: US$14.9 MILLION).FY GROUP ADJUSTED EBITDA LOSS OF APPROXIMATELY US$3.2 MILLION (2018: US$1.2 MILLION LOSS).FY REDUCTION IN CORPORATE COSTS TO US$1.8 MILLION (2018: US$2.7 MILLION).FY SALES VOLUMES OF PREMIUM QUALITY SUPERFINE TRANSFORMER OIL AND BASE OIL OF 18.3 MILLION LITRES (2018: 23.0 MILLION LITRES).COMPANY CONTINUES TO WORK ON A REFINANCING PACKAGE IN RESPECT OF THECANTON PLANT AND ASSETS IN EARLY PART OF 2020.CONFIRM THAT HYDRODEC HAS SIGNED A 3-YEAR CONTRACT WITH DUKE ENERGY.REVISED ITS EXPECTATIONS FOR 2020 TO BE MATERIALLY LOWER THAN PREVIOUS MARKET EXPECTATIONS FOR THIS YEAR.BOARD EXPECTS AN IMPROVEMENT ON FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR 2019 WITH GROUP TARGETING POSITIVE EBITDA FROM US OPERATIONS FOR 2020.HYDRODEC GROUP- WILL CONTINUE TO PURSUE OTHER STRATEGIC GROWTH INITIATIVES THAT WILL ULTIMATELY SEEK TO ACCELERATE GROUP'S OVERALL PROFITABILITY."}
